From 01a0543ea2cc45738f9783d777e963743bb899e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:59:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/16] trail-rules: a trail becomes a rule only past a seeded
 null on a held-out third; the rules about rules as data

Pure kernel module (promoteRoute, promoteHead, ruleEntry, META_RULES). 10 tests, including a
control built to fail: 0 of 600 chance-label route-tests promoted. Power measured on synthetic labels
(needs ~60-120 deposits for a 0.9 v 0.1 gap, 240 for 0.8 v 0.3). ruleEntry shapes an entry; nothing is woven.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AP2eRC5CScKTs8ZE4Wpdoe
---
