Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:30:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/16] quote-frames: a codec registers its own table; marks
 the table does not know are a typed gap that lists them

Found by running Genesis in 65 languages: 35 editions mark no quotation at all, 25 mark them and had no table,
and the Spanish table found 0 of 224 straight-quote spans without saying so. registerQuoteTable (a built-in cannot be
replaced), marks_outside_table and no_quote_table now carry the marks seen; straight quotes read in fra/spa/ita/rus.
ingestDocument reports the lang it used. 28 tests.

