From 4e9ff854b9a6c4670a64a8b93c1300c1ed0b24c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 01:39:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/16] chat: the mark-free speech layer: reported speech from
 a verb of saying, no quotation marks needed

speech-frames.js reads UD rows (codec-neutral) and decides by position, not by tree (the parser inverts unmarked speech:
advcl/parataxis from the quoted clause). Speech verbs come from the act prior's VerbNet 37.x readings (at least half of a verb's
readings), never a list. Coordinated clauses after the speech are UNKNOWN, a marked quotation's tag opens nothing, a missing
prior is a typed gap. ingest.mjs adds reported/reportedBy/reportedHead/mode per verb; askFramed says whose words an answer is.
Falsified against the aligned marked edition (Genesis, English-WEB marks vs KJV, no marks): fresh sample P 89% R 82%,
diagnosis sample P 92% R 84% (before the predicate fix P 77% R 88%; baseline before this layer: 0 verbs framed in KJV).
Found and fixed by the oracle: any-class-in-37 made go and dwell speech verbs. 16 tests; chat suite 150, 110 pass, same 2 failures.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AP2eRC5CScKTs8ZE4Wpdoe
