From 8f0010a179622390974f48f2e75a93994704615d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 01:47:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/16] frames: one layer, two doors; the canonical reader now
 says who holds the words

The quote and speech layers move from chat/ to adapters/text/ (beside speakers.js) so the canonical reader does not import a surface.
frames-layer.js is the one implementation; chat/ingest.mjs and the new the-fold/read-framed.mjs (readDocument rows:true + frames) both call it.
Language must be declared (a missing or unheld language is a typed gap, never English). Aligning the doors found and fixed two bugs:
a quotation that closed in the PREVIOUS paragraph was taken for the tag of the next paragraph's speech verb; and a quotation that continues into the
next paragraph swallowed the narration after its last mark (a paragraph break now ends every open quotation, typed as continuing).
Proof (native/tests/read-framed.test.mjs, 7 tests): 17 of 17 hand-labelled verbs through the canonical door; chat and canonical doors agree on 17 of 17;
Genesis oracle through the canonical door: P 87% R 80% (fresh), P 88% R 86% (other); clause tree agrees with the position rule on 73 of its 80 speech sentences.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AP2eRC5CScKTs8ZE4Wpdoe
