From 1ec779f62aa1ef047f4e2aac9e5434fb09134c99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 03:16:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/16] name-smell: does a surface smell like a name? measured
 from the text's casing, the POS prior and the parser's tag in context; no
 list

Both cast builders take capitalised sentence-openers and common words for names, each differently (71 agree, 8 only canonical, 18 only chat on 5 texts).
The rule: a closed-class word is never a name; a word also lowercase in the text is a common word; a name is capitalised away from a sentence start;
the parser's contextual tag can only remove a name; all-caps tokens are their own word. Gating both builders with it: name agreement Jaccard 0.73 -> 0.95,
all 12 junk words kept out, but only 3 of 6 eye-labelled real names admitted (Cush and Manasseh mis-tagged by the parser, On vetoed as an adposition).
Not wired into either builder. 11 tests. The pinned emergent-smell was tried first and is the wrong instrument (671 word types, knew none of 22 real names).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AP2eRC5CScKTs8ZE4Wpdoe
---
 native/adapters/text/name-smell.js       | 51 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 native/adapters/text/name-smell.test.mjs | 55 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 package.json                             |  2 +-
 3 files changed, 107 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 native/adapters/text/name-smell.js
