From d8d979b29d3f8a496b794d8437cc62a2f8435344 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:41:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/16] name-smell v2: a weighted joint model, ablated and
 gated; replaces the rule cascade (still not wired into any builder)

The v1 veto cascade could not survive casual speech or typos and could not be outvoted. v2: every signal is a weight on one log-odds score, the prior is a Bayesian offset,
casing evidence is scaled by the document's own casing reliability, the answer is a probability with a standard deviation and a certainty (Laplace covariance).
Gate (native/scripts/ablate-name-smell-loto.mjs): fit on an INDEPENDENT hand-labelled gold, leave-one-text-family-out, backward elimination with bootstrap intervals.
The first fit on weak treebank labels was CIRCULAR (the parser's tag shares the treebank) and looked too good (lowercase AUC above clean, casing weight negative): not shipped.
Held-out AUC 0.994 clean / 0.954 lowercase / 0.973 case noise / 0.993 typos / 0.981 ALL vs 0.716 capitalisation and 0.949 prior alone; unattested names only 0.835.
Signal 'repeat' dropped (credibly harmful on lowercase). Cast-level, threshold-free: AUC 0.898 vs 0.853 for v1 on both builders' proposed names. Largest covariance eigenvalue 1.26 -> 0.044 as evidence grows.
Known: confident errors for a surname that is also a common word (Long), for capitalised KJV common nouns (Seas, Cherubs); gold is one labeller, 5 texts; English only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AP2eRC5CScKTs8ZE4Wpdoe
