+// These two kinds are PROPOSALS (no other repo declares them yet): whoever writes them declares them, and khora reads whichever exist.
+// ORDER IS CAUSAL, NOT THE CLOCK (owner, 2026-11-26: "the writing order is less important than the dependency order and what the light cone was of the writer at submission"). Every entry records what its writer had SEEN when it was
+// submitted (`seen`, `of`); a verdict REVISES another exactly when the other is in its light cone, whatever the timestamps say. The live verdicts at an address are the pharos's causal HEADS (lib heads: entries that no other live
+// entry has seen). One head is the verdict. Several heads that AGREE are the verdict. Several heads that DISAGREE are writers who never saw each other: that is a typed gap `verdict_conflict` (the ids and the values), the nomination
+// stands, and nothing is picked by timestamp. A RETRACTED verdict stops counting (the pharos skips it); a verdict at a cell outside Interpretation, or `of` an entry that is no longer the current nomination, is NOT applied and is a typed gap.
 // The nomination is never edited: each frame keeps its own `framed`/`reported`, and gains `effective` ({ reported, source: "verdict" | "nomination" }) and `judged` (the verdict's id and cell, or null).
 import { pathToFileURL } from "node:url";
